   "source": [
    "##The anomaly detection analysis applies three unsupervised algorithms: Isolation Forest, Local Outlier Factor (LOF) and robust Mahalanobis distance.\n",
    "The use of multiple algorithms is appropriate because the dataset does not contain verified anomaly labels. Each algorithm identifies unusual observations using different statistical assumptions.\n",
    "Isolation Forest identifies observations that can be isolated more easily than typical observations.\n",
    "Local Outlier Factor identifies observations with substantially different local density compared with their neighbouring observations.\n",
    "Robust Mahalanobis distance identifies observations that deviate significantly from the multivariate distribution of the data.\n",
    "Combining these approaches provides a broader perspective on unusual transaction behaviour than relying on a single detection algorithm.\n",
    "4.2 Interpretation of rule-based inconsistencies\n",
    "The rule-based detection layer identifies the following operational inconsistencies:\n",
    "Business rule\tOrders flagged\n",
    "Payment mismatch\t216\n",
    "Freight greater than product price\t3,159\n",
    "Inconsistent timestamps\t166\n",
    "Delivery delay exceeding 30 days\t360\n",
    "These results highlight different potential areas of operational risk.\n",
    "Payment mismatches: The 216 flagged transactions exhibit differences between recorded payment values and the combined product and freight amounts. These may indicate payment reconciliation problems, recording errors or unusual payment arrangements.\n",
    "However, payment vouchers and other legitimate adjustments can create valid differences, meaning that these observations require verification rather than automatic classification as fraudulent.\n",
    "Freight greater than product price: The 3,159 flagged transactions have freight costs exceeding product prices. This may indicate unusually expensive shipping arrangements, potentially affecting affordability and customer satisfaction. Such transactions may be legitimate for bulky products, distant destinations or specialised delivery services.\n",
    "Inconsistent timestamps: The 166 flagged orders contain delivery or carrier timestamps that precede the purchase date. These observations suggest possible data-entry errors, system recording problems or inconsistencies in timestamp processing.\n",
    "Extremely late deliveries: The 360 transactions with delivery delays exceeding 30 days represent potentially significant fulfilment failures. These cases warrant operational investigation because extended delivery delays can negatively affect customer satisfaction and marketplace trust.\n",
    "4.3 Interpretation of anomaly detection agreement and stability\n",
    "The Jaccard similarity results between the three anomaly detection algorithms are relatively low:\n",
    "Isolation Forest versus LOF: 0.05.\n",
    "Isolation Forest versus Mahalanobis: 0.09.\n",
    "LOF versus Mahalanobis: 0.15.\n",
    "This indicates limited agreement regarding which individual transactions are anomalous.\n",
    "The low agreement is not necessarily a methodological failure. Instead, it reflects the different assumptions used by the algorithms. An observation may be unusual in its local neighbourhood without being globally extreme, or it may deviate from a multivariate distribution without being isolated easily by a tree-based algorithm.\n",
    "The Isolation Forest stability assessment produces a Spearman correlation of 0.99 across random seeds and a top-1% overlap of 0.86. This indicates that its ranking is highly consistent across repeated runs.\n",
    "The combined anomaly score identifies:\n",
    "493 orders within the top 0.5%.\n",
    "986 orders within the top 1.0%.\n",
    "1,973 orders within the top 2.0%.\n",
    "Using the top 1% as the primary anomaly threshold provides a manageable initial review population while retaining the most unusual observations.\n",
    "4.4 Interpretation of proxy validation\n",
    "The proxy validation provides particularly important evidence regarding the operational relevance of the detected anomalies.\n",
    "Indicator\tNon-flagged orders\tFlagged orders\n",
    "Number of orders\t97,679\t987\n",
    "Cancellation rate\t0.5%\t0.6%\n",
    "Late-delivery rate\t7.9%\t33.4%\n",
    "Mean review score\t4.117\t2.906\n",
    "The results demonstrate substantial differences in delivery performance and customer satisfaction.\n",
    "Flagged orders have a late-delivery rate of 33.4%, compared with 7.9% among non-flagged orders. This represents approximately a 4.2-fold difference in observed late-delivery rates.\n",
    "Similarly, flagged orders record a substantially lower average review score of 2.91 compared with 4.12 for non-flagged orders.\n",
    "These findings suggest that the anomaly detection framework is identifying transactions associated with operationally undesirable outcomes.\n",
    "However, cancellation rates are relatively similar between the two groups, suggesting that the anomalies are more strongly associated with delivery and customer-experience challenges than with cancellations.\n",
    "It is important to emphasise that these indicators are proxy validation measures rather than verified anomaly labels. Consequently, the results demonstrate operational relevance but do not establish fraud, misconduct or deliberate manipulation.\n",
    "4.5 Interpretation of anomaly categories and operational implications\n",
    "The flagged transactions are classified according to their dominant contributing features.\n",
    "Anomaly category\tFlagged orders\tOperational interpretation\n",
    "Logistics cost\t350\tUnusual freight charges or shipping-cost structures\n",
    "Delivery\t321\tExtended delivery periods or unusual delivery delays\n",
    "Customer experience\t162\tTransactions associated with unusually low review scores\n",
    "Payment\t106\tPotential payment discrepancies or unusual instalment patterns\n",
    "Basket\t18\tUnusual item or seller combinations\n",
    "Product size\t15\tUnusual product weight or volume characteristics\n",
    "Pricing\t15\tUnusual product pricing behaviour\n",
    "The results indicate that logistics cost and delivery-related anomalies represent the largest categories, together accounting for 671 flagged orders.\n",
    "This suggests that logistics efficiency and delivery reliability should receive priority attention during operational investigations.\n",
