    "Human oversight: Anomaly flags should trigger further investigation rather than automatic accusations or punitive decisions.\n",
    "Predictive uncertainty: Forecasts should be accompanied by appropriate uncertainty estimates, particularly for long-distance deliveries and geographical regions with limited observations.\n",
    "Model drift: Delivery patterns can change over time. Models should therefore be periodically evaluated and retrained using more recent operational data.\n",
    "Causal interpretation: Statistical associations and SHAP explanations describe observed relationships and model behaviour; they do not independently establish causal effects.\n",
    "Final recommendation\n",
